-- title:
--   No proper generalisations of ξ_∞, ξ₀ in the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $N_0 \ne 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` for the level-$(N_0,q)$ Igusa model, whose structural morphism is `toBase N₀ q : X N₀ q ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of (DRLevel.R q))`. Let $O$ be a commutative local ring equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O \colon \mathrm{DRLevel.R}\, q \to O$, and assume that the maximal ideal of $O$ is the ideal generated by the image of $q$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $t \colon O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O =$ `DRLevel.XO ρO` for the base change of `X N₀ q` along $\rho_O$, with structural morphism `DRLevel.XO.toBase ρO` given by the second projection of the pullback to $\operatorname{Spec} O$, and let $\xi_\infty =$ `𝔛.ξinf ρO toκ` and $\xi_0 =$ `𝔛.ξzero ρO toκ` be the two points of $X_O$ attached by the package to $\rho_O$ and $t$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two statements: for every point $y$ of $X_O$ lying outside the preimage under `DRLevel.XO.toBase ρO` of the basic open subset $D(q) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} O$, if $\xi_\infty$ lies in the closure of $\{y\}$ then $y = \xi_\infty$; and likewise, if $\xi_0$ lies in the closure of $\{y\}$ then $y = \xi_0$.
--
--   Since the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $q$, the points excluded by the open condition are exactly those of the special fibre of $X_O$, so the assertion is that $\xi_\infty$ and $\xi_0$ admit no proper generalisation inside that fibre, i.e. each is the generic point of an irreducible component of the special fibre. It is used in the study of the crossings of the two components and of the branch ideals on the regular model, for instance by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.not_branchIdeal_le_branchIdeal_crossingPt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.not_branchIdeal_le_branchIdeal_crossingPt) and [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam).
